WEBVTT

00:02.380 --> 00:04.050
I figured this was coming...

00:04.050 --> 00:05.600
What do you mean?

00:06.080 --> 00:10.320
<i>After dealing with the lizardmen and 
the werewolves, here come the orcs.</i>

00:10.320 --> 00:14.530
<i>Their leader is a big deal, and made a 
fortune on the excavation of mana stones.</i>

00:14.860 --> 00:17.170
<i>It's been a month since I opened the clinic,</i>

00:17.170 --> 00:21.850
<i>and after this, I'll have dealt with the 
leaders of all the factions in the slums.</i>

00:22.420 --> 00:25.790
Out of curiosity, would you say
your boss can be reasoned with?

00:26.060 --> 00:30.590
Lady Loewe is as wise as she is dignified.

00:31.010 --> 00:32.630
I sure hope so.

00:33.130 --> 00:36.220
<i>Zophia's been dropping off 
extravagant gifts every day...</i>

00:36.700 --> 00:41.100
<i>And Lynga's been building a massive "palace" 
next door to make up for the mess she made.</i>

00:41.630 --> 00:43.430
<i>But if the head of the orcs is reasonable,</i>

00:43.430 --> 00:45.530
<i>I shouldn't need to worry 
about that kind of thing.</i>

00:45.530 --> 00:47.730
So why didn't she come in person?

00:48.280 --> 00:52.030
There have been lizardmen and werewolves 
coming and going from this place.

00:52.030 --> 00:56.200
Do you really think I'd bring Lady 
Loewe to a place in enemy territory?

00:59.160 --> 01:00.200
How serious is it?

01:00.610 --> 01:02.160
She can't be moved.

01:05.360 --> 01:06.970
You should've led with that.

02:41.660 --> 02:42.900
In here.

02:47.760 --> 02:51.320
Lady Loewe, I've brought Zenos, 
the underground healer.

02:51.320 --> 02:52.480
Good of you to come.

02:53.040 --> 02:54.360
I am Loewe.

02:55.080 --> 02:56.700
So you're Loewe.

02:56.700 --> 02:58.320
How'd you hear about me?

02:58.320 --> 02:59.780
How could I not have?

02:59.780 --> 03:02.720
You're a celebrity to those who dwell 
in the underworld of the slums.

03:03.080 --> 03:04.450
Wow, really?

03:04.450 --> 03:06.710
The lizardmen and werewolves were raving,

03:06.710 --> 03:11.360
"There's this awesome healer! But I can't 
tell you about him or he'll attract trouble!"

03:11.360 --> 03:14.210
So I looked into you myself.

03:14.510 --> 03:17.010
<i>Damn it, what part of 
"underground operation"</i>

03:17.010 --> 03:19.300
<i>made them want to spread 
my name around like that?!</i>

03:19.300 --> 03:24.470
I'm told that you can provide any kind of 
healing as long as the price paid is equal.

03:25.120 --> 03:27.610
I've gotten tired of 
working for free, you see.

03:27.610 --> 03:32.270
Well, I find myself unable to move from 
here at the moment. Can you tell why?

03:32.650 --> 03:35.350
<i>Is this a test? I guess I'll have to check.</i>

03:38.650 --> 03:39.690
Scan.

03:40.480 --> 03:41.950
What are you doing?

03:41.950 --> 03:45.120
I don't see any external injuries, 
so I'm looking inside you.

03:45.410 --> 03:47.870
I've never heard of a 
healer who can do that.

03:48.350 --> 03:52.540
I'm curious how they heal anyone if they 
don't check what's going on inside.

03:54.580 --> 03:56.690
There's a lump in your abdomen.

03:56.690 --> 03:58.150
And I can sense mana...

03:58.660 --> 03:59.800
Is it a mana stone?

04:00.200 --> 04:01.820
Correct you are.

04:01.820 --> 04:04.800
Enchanted for Explosion at a 
particularly high potency, at that.

04:05.050 --> 04:07.640
Wait, did someone slip this in your food?

04:07.640 --> 04:10.930
Not at all! I mistook it for a 
rice ball and ate it, is all.

04:10.930 --> 04:11.760
So you're an idiot.

04:11.760 --> 04:14.250
Despite appearances, 
I have quite the appetite!

04:14.250 --> 04:15.690
I don't care!

04:15.690 --> 04:19.530
This is ridiculous. You'll expel it 
sooner or later without any help.

04:19.530 --> 04:21.070
I'm afraid not.

04:21.070 --> 04:25.440
I partially chewed it apart, so there's 
not much time until it detonates.

04:25.440 --> 04:28.470
Not to mention, if I move carelessly, 
that could also set it off.

04:28.470 --> 04:30.200
So that's why you can't move.

04:30.200 --> 04:34.040
The real problem is that my 
men refuse to leave my side.

04:34.590 --> 04:35.560
Chief!

04:35.560 --> 04:37.200
When we die, we die together!

04:37.200 --> 04:39.340
We'll be at your side!

04:39.750 --> 04:41.680
And what do you expect me to do?

04:41.680 --> 04:44.430
I'm looking to donate our wealth to you.

04:44.780 --> 04:48.350
Should this stone detonate, it will spell 
the end for the orcs in the slums.

04:48.840 --> 04:51.060
I'd rather give our accumulated 
wealth to someone

04:51.060 --> 04:53.990
who'd make good use of it
than let it be plundered.

04:53.990 --> 04:57.130
I've heard that, while you demand 
high prices for your healing,

04:57.130 --> 04:59.570
you're willing to see children for free.

04:59.570 --> 05:02.480
I'm fond of children myself.

05:06.500 --> 05:09.190
And you ingested this mana stone recently?

05:09.190 --> 05:10.080
Yes.

05:10.800 --> 05:11.680
Scalpel.

05:13.960 --> 05:14.650
Hey...

05:15.740 --> 05:16.960
Don't move, now.

05:16.960 --> 05:18.460
Bastard!

05:16.960 --> 05:18.460
What do you think you're doing?!

05:20.920 --> 05:23.630
Wh-What did you just do?

05:24.420 --> 05:26.900
I opened your stomach to 
extract the mana stone.

05:26.900 --> 05:29.600
And then I healed it shut.

05:29.600 --> 05:32.310
Without a license, this is 
about all I can manage.

05:32.780 --> 05:35.400
The fact that you can do 
it at all is incredible...

05:36.220 --> 05:38.190
If you're not careful, it could detonate!

05:38.550 --> 05:39.810
Oh, right.

05:48.450 --> 05:50.320
N-Not so much as a scratch?!

05:50.320 --> 05:52.720
I protected my hands with defensive magic.

05:52.720 --> 05:55.250
It still hurt, though, so I had to heal them.

05:55.830 --> 05:56.890
We're done here.

05:57.720 --> 05:59.790
You can have the key back.

06:00.680 --> 06:05.670
Incredible. If you had stayed quiet, our 
entire fortune would have been yours.

06:06.020 --> 06:08.910
I only demand a price equal to 
the amount of work I need to do.

06:08.910 --> 06:10.670
That would've been too much in this case.

06:13.810 --> 06:16.540
I like you, Zenos the underground healer!

06:16.540 --> 06:18.880
You've earned a great debt 
from the orcish race today!

06:18.880 --> 06:22.540
Should you need our help, 
just call, and you'll have it!

06:22.540 --> 06:24.090
I'd really prefer you kept your distance.

06:24.090 --> 06:25.610
No need for modesty!

06:25.610 --> 06:30.150
We can provide around-the-clock 
security for your clinic, if you'd like!

06:30.150 --> 06:32.000
Seriously, don't!

06:33.290 --> 06:35.430
Anyway, the moment I relaxed, 
my appetite came back.

06:35.790 --> 06:38.540
Care to join me for some rice balls, Zenos?

06:38.540 --> 06:40.390
Maybe you could eat something else?

06:45.210 --> 06:47.730
What's got you making that sullen face?

06:47.730 --> 06:52.430
Just thinking that Zophia, Lynga, 
and Loewe have been visiting a lot lately.

06:53.060 --> 06:55.930
Now that you mention it, I guess they have.

06:56.510 --> 06:58.230
Zophia on the day of the moon.

06:58.570 --> 07:00.310
Lynga on the day of water.

07:00.560 --> 07:02.270
Loewe on the day of gold.

07:02.580 --> 07:05.750
And they're never injured. 
Why do they bother?

07:05.750 --> 07:09.070
Do you really have no idea at all, Zenos?

07:09.070 --> 07:10.730
They must really be bored.

07:10.730 --> 07:13.820
I don't think that's it...

07:13.820 --> 07:15.200
It sounds like love.

07:15.560 --> 07:17.110
How long have you been there?

07:18.310 --> 07:21.290
These women are infatuated with you.

07:21.290 --> 07:24.460
What? Don't be ridiculous. There's no way.

07:24.460 --> 07:27.670
I'm a totally unremarkable underground 
healer who doesn't even have a license.

07:27.670 --> 07:29.680
There's no fooling my eyes.

07:29.680 --> 07:32.100
Whenever I watch from the ceiling,

07:32.100 --> 07:34.490
their eyes betray their lovesickness.

07:34.490 --> 07:36.960
You learn how to tell these 
things after living 300 years.

07:36.960 --> 07:38.430
Uh, you're not "living," though.

07:38.430 --> 07:41.200
I'm kind of worried.

07:41.200 --> 07:43.150
They're all so pretty...

07:43.150 --> 07:45.270
And they're all huge weirdos.

07:46.790 --> 07:49.590
It's only a matter of time before the three

07:49.590 --> 07:53.140
demihuman factions wage 
a war over Zenos, I'd say.

07:53.140 --> 07:54.280
That's absurd.

07:54.540 --> 07:59.200
Lily, try and do your best 
to amuse me, like them.

07:59.450 --> 08:02.490
B-But I'm only a kid.

08:02.490 --> 08:05.100
I'm not sexy like them...

08:07.090 --> 08:09.760
All maidens in love are beautiful.

08:10.050 --> 08:12.760
Th-Thank you, Carmilla!

08:13.200 --> 08:16.140
<i>The three demihuman leaders 
fighting over me?</i>

08:16.770 --> 08:19.140
That's so ridiculous I can't even laugh.

08:21.140 --> 08:24.770
Doc, I'm thinking of declaring 
war on the others.

08:24.770 --> 08:27.730
Would you be willing to 
side with the lizardmen?

08:27.730 --> 08:28.570
Say what?

08:28.570 --> 08:31.900
A war over Zenos...

08:33.990 --> 08:37.510
Sir Zenos! The time has come to 
settle things with the others.

08:37.510 --> 08:39.280
I want you to side with the werewolves!

08:39.280 --> 08:40.410
Uh, hang on...

08:40.730 --> 08:43.210
Zenos, the time has come to wipe out the—

08:43.210 --> 08:44.460
Okay, hold up!

08:47.000 --> 08:50.590
The fighting's supposed to begin at 
noon on the next day of ground...

08:52.280 --> 08:55.500
All-out war between all three factions.

08:55.500 --> 08:58.760
So many will die because 
of your womanizing ways.

08:59.080 --> 09:01.600
I really don't appreciate 
the way you put that.

09:03.910 --> 09:06.560
And what are you pouting about, Lily?

09:15.390 --> 09:18.480
You actually had the guts 
to show up only to die.

09:18.480 --> 09:21.990
Today we're gonna settle who 
deserves to be on top around here.

09:22.390 --> 09:23.810
That's so funny!

09:23.810 --> 09:28.540
Because you're about to find out how much 
Lynga has been taking it easy on you two.

09:28.540 --> 09:30.090
Such foolishness.

09:30.090 --> 09:32.880
Do you really think you'll be able to 
stand against orcs in mortal combat?

09:32.880 --> 09:34.840
You will both be dying today.

09:36.020 --> 09:37.840
Hold it right there!

09:39.360 --> 09:41.010
Zenos?

09:39.360 --> 09:41.010
Doc?

09:39.360 --> 09:41.010
Sir Zenos?

09:41.010 --> 09:44.320
Now, I'm not here to stop this fight.

09:45.430 --> 09:49.150
I know you three have long-standing 
grudges after years of conflict.

09:49.570 --> 09:52.860
So I want you to have it out 
until you're all satisfied.

09:52.860 --> 09:54.230
That's all I wanted to say.

09:56.480 --> 09:59.280
Looks like we've got Doc's approval.

09:59.280 --> 10:01.620
So let's go all-out.

10:02.090 --> 10:05.660
And whoever survives can 
claim him. What do you say?

10:05.660 --> 10:08.620
You're on! He's already 
Lynga's, in that case.

10:08.900 --> 10:11.630
Zenos's chastity will be mine!

10:11.630 --> 10:14.560
Is that true, Zenos?

10:14.560 --> 10:16.880
That wasn't part of the deal, no.

11:08.810 --> 11:11.690
What is it? They just won't stay down!

11:11.690 --> 11:15.230
Doesn't matter how bad we beat 
them, they just keep getting up!

11:15.600 --> 11:18.650
Pretty sure we've cut at 
least 30 of them down...

11:19.980 --> 11:20.860
What the...

11:21.330 --> 11:23.620
My wounds just healed.

11:23.620 --> 11:27.360
Like I said, I'm not here to stop your fight.

11:27.360 --> 11:28.860
You're free to keep going.

11:28.860 --> 11:32.050
But you're also my patients.

11:32.050 --> 11:34.250
So when you're hurt, I'm gonna heal you.

11:34.550 --> 11:37.090
I am an underground healer, after all.

11:37.670 --> 11:39.160
That explains it.

11:39.160 --> 11:42.310
Well, I sure feel like a fool after all that.

11:43.590 --> 11:47.850
I guess you've been working this 
entire time, haven't you, Doc?

11:48.240 --> 11:52.240
But I've never heard of a healer who 
could heal so many people instantly

11:52.240 --> 11:53.560
over such a long time!

11:53.930 --> 11:57.410
He told us to have at it, but I never 
thought he could heal us all...

11:58.000 --> 12:00.690
But at this rate, the fighting will never end.

12:00.690 --> 12:03.630
Exactly. There'll be no end to it.

12:03.630 --> 12:06.550
"He hit me, so I'll get revenge."

12:06.550 --> 12:09.640
"He kicked me, so I'll get revenge."

12:09.640 --> 12:11.410
It never ends.

12:11.760 --> 12:13.120
So do you want to keep going?

12:13.120 --> 12:15.580
Because if you do, I'm going to be right here.

12:15.580 --> 12:17.920
And rest assured, I will be 
getting paid for all this.

12:23.060 --> 12:24.800
He's got a point.

12:24.800 --> 12:26.360
There'll be no end to this.

12:26.360 --> 12:29.060
What are we even doing?

12:29.060 --> 12:31.500
It seems silly now.

12:31.500 --> 12:33.980
All we're doing is making ourselves tired.

12:34.400 --> 12:37.830
I honestly feel satisfied 
after all that fighting.

12:41.290 --> 12:42.540
It is what it is.

12:42.540 --> 12:45.840
And given what Doc just said, 
we might as well wrap this up for today.

12:45.840 --> 12:47.410
No objections from the werewolves!

12:47.410 --> 12:49.080
"Forgiveness is strength."

12:49.080 --> 12:51.080
An old orcish proverb.

12:51.550 --> 12:55.080
Sounds like we've only got one 
reason to fight going forward.

12:55.080 --> 12:57.580
Lynga has the advantage with that one!

12:57.580 --> 13:00.420
And that's the one battle I won't yield on.

13:00.870 --> 13:03.380
What do you think they're talking about?

13:04.800 --> 13:07.440
You really are popular, Zenos...

13:07.900 --> 13:10.940
Why'd you do this, though?

13:11.800 --> 13:13.890
There's something my mentor told me once.

13:14.320 --> 13:16.720
"A healer is third-rate if 
they just heal injuries,

13:16.720 --> 13:18.510
second-rate if they can 
wholly heal a person,

13:18.510 --> 13:20.650
and first-rate if they can 
make the world a better place."

13:21.090 --> 13:24.590
What was your mentor like?

13:24.590 --> 13:27.620
A weirdo. But really impressive.

13:28.490 --> 13:30.590
Which is why, third-rate as I might be,

13:30.590 --> 13:34.080
I want to try to improve things in the slums.

13:34.430 --> 13:36.830
That's so cool, Zenos!

13:36.830 --> 13:38.490
Or at least, that's what I'll say.

13:38.490 --> 13:39.500
It's just talk?

13:40.100 --> 13:44.160
Think about it. They're all regular 
patients at our run-down clinic.

13:44.160 --> 13:46.620
We can't risk losing them over this nonsense.

13:48.020 --> 13:49.220
You liar.

13:49.980 --> 13:52.980
<i>He knows that if everyone gets along,</i>

13:52.980 --> 13:56.020
<i>there'll be fewer injuries, 
and fewer patients.</i>

13:59.120 --> 14:00.630
Hey, Zenos.

14:00.630 --> 14:01.650
What's up?

14:02.020 --> 14:04.780
I like you, Zenos.

14:05.850 --> 14:07.360
I like you, too, Lily.

14:09.120 --> 14:11.880
That's not what I mean when I say, "I like you"!

14:11.880 --> 14:13.820
Then what exactly do you mean?

14:13.820 --> 14:15.750
N-Never mind!

14:19.950 --> 14:22.440
Well, time to get paid and go home.

14:22.440 --> 14:24.130
You're still gonna charge them?

14:24.430 --> 14:29.430
Of course. Do you know how much work 
it is to heal this many people?

14:29.430 --> 14:31.220
That means I need to collect my fee.

14:32.500 --> 14:35.970
You think Carmilla will be sad nobody died?

14:35.970 --> 14:38.940
Maybe. It'd serve her right, though.

14:39.340 --> 14:42.060
I think... she'll actually be happy, though.

14:50.830 --> 14:53.090
You called for me, Division Commander?

14:53.090 --> 14:56.160
I was waiting, Vice Commander Krishna.

14:56.160 --> 14:58.910
I wasn't expecting the summons. 
Has something happened?

14:58.910 --> 15:03.550
Yes. I've heard some 
concerning rumors lately.

15:03.550 --> 15:04.500
What rumors?

15:04.500 --> 15:09.590
Apparently, the turf war between the 
demihumans of the slums has calmed down.

15:09.960 --> 15:17.560
But the lizardmen, werewolves, and orcs have 
been feuding over territory for years now.

15:17.560 --> 15:20.810
I have a hard time believing 
that it'd suddenly cool off.

15:22.490 --> 15:26.400
But on the off-chance that it 
might be true, we can't ignore it.

15:26.400 --> 15:29.920
The Kingdom of Herzeth has prospered

15:29.920 --> 15:33.490
under its strict hierarchical system,
 with the royals at the top.

15:33.780 --> 15:35.890
The citizens take out their 
frustrations on the poor.

15:35.890 --> 15:37.790
And the poor take out their frustrations by

15:37.790 --> 15:40.240
squabbling among themselves, 
specifically among different races.

15:40.240 --> 15:42.320
That's how we maintain equilibrium.

15:42.320 --> 15:46.750
But suppose the poor 
presented a united front...

15:47.080 --> 15:50.210
You believe they'd pose a threat to 
the citizens, the aristocracy...

15:50.210 --> 15:51.680
maybe even the ruling class?

15:52.020 --> 15:53.300
Exactly.

15:53.740 --> 15:55.180
The king is like the sun to our people,

15:55.180 --> 15:59.680
and it is the duty of the royal order of knights 
to defend the capital where our ruler dwells.

15:59.960 --> 16:04.690
But Commander, the three demihuman 
races have been feuding for so long.

16:05.530 --> 16:08.440
There's no way such deep-seated 
grudges could be forgiven so easily.

16:08.790 --> 16:12.700
The rumors say that a third 
party mediated between them.

16:12.990 --> 16:14.700
That seems even more implausible.

16:15.180 --> 16:19.980
Zophia the Tornado, Lynga the 
Tyrant, and Loewe the Mighty...

16:19.980 --> 16:22.540
They're dangerous, major 
figures in the underworld.

16:22.540 --> 16:26.000
I can't imagine an individual 
capable of corralling them.

16:26.410 --> 16:28.720
I feel the same way.

16:28.720 --> 16:33.590
But we can't ignore even the possibility 
that the rumors might be true.

16:33.870 --> 16:36.470
And that's why you called for me?

16:36.790 --> 16:40.100
This is an issue that could 
threaten the state of our nation.

16:40.100 --> 16:41.890
I can't leave that to the rank and file.

16:42.480 --> 16:45.480
I want you, my vice commander, to handle this.

16:45.890 --> 16:47.230
I'll see to it, sir.

16:47.770 --> 16:50.440
I'm counting on you, Iron Rose.

16:50.440 --> 16:55.480
If such an individual does exist, 
I will apprehend him.

16:58.530 --> 16:59.740
Zenos—

16:58.530 --> 17:00.630
Sir Zenos! Is it a cold?

17:00.630 --> 17:02.900
Lynga can warm you up with her tail!

17:02.900 --> 17:05.220
That should be my job.

17:05.220 --> 17:09.000
My muscles are warmer than you'd think, 
plus there's my bosom to consider.

17:09.820 --> 17:13.920
I... don't have a tail.

17:14.210 --> 17:16.770
Or muscles...

17:16.770 --> 17:19.430
Or... bosom.

17:20.510 --> 17:22.520
I'm gonna put some tea on!

17:22.900 --> 17:24.450
You're all way too protective!

17:24.450 --> 17:26.430
It was just a sneeze.

17:26.430 --> 17:28.900
I'm trying to heal someone, so quiet down.

17:31.890 --> 17:35.530
Your healing will never 
cease to amaze me, Doc.

17:35.810 --> 17:39.950
Come to think of it, you haven't needed 
healing in a while, huh, Zophia?

17:39.950 --> 17:41.520
Oh, come on, Lily!

17:41.520 --> 17:45.330
That makes it sounds like I'm always 
here when I'm not a patient!

17:45.330 --> 17:47.000
That is literally the case.

17:47.490 --> 17:52.000
Just so you know, I got this 
injury while I was working.

17:52.260 --> 17:54.630
Oh, right. You're a thief, aren't you?

17:56.030 --> 17:58.250
I'm pretty selective about 
my targets, but yeah...

17:58.250 --> 18:01.300
And the royal order of knights 
has their eye on us now.

18:01.300 --> 18:05.310
Had a bit of a scrap with them 
yesterday, which is how I got hurt.

18:05.310 --> 18:09.550
Come to think of it, you had 
both injured your arms before.

18:09.550 --> 18:11.650
Did the royal knights do that?

18:11.650 --> 18:13.010
Yeah, they did.

18:13.010 --> 18:16.710
One of 'em got me when we were 
sneaking into an aristocrat's manor.

18:16.710 --> 18:18.890
They got my arm, too, Sis.

18:18.890 --> 18:22.010
The crazy woman blasted me with 
that flame magic gun out of nowhere.

18:22.010 --> 18:22.990
A crazy woman?

18:22.990 --> 18:25.490
I think she's their vice commander?

18:25.490 --> 18:29.190
Some crazy chick they call the Iron Rose.

18:29.190 --> 18:32.810
She unleashes real hell, all with 
a blank expression on her face.

18:32.810 --> 18:34.590
The Iron Rose...

18:36.060 --> 18:39.410
Imagine the trouble that getting 
her attention would cause,

18:39.410 --> 18:42.350
especially with the surplus of 
dangerous women we already have.

18:43.550 --> 18:46.310
I'm... the normal one, right?

18:47.300 --> 18:49.260
I doubt I have to worry.

18:49.260 --> 18:54.980
Why would the high and mighty royal knights 
care about some nobody underground healer?

18:55.280 --> 18:58.050
My wraith's instinct is 
usually pretty accurate...

18:58.050 --> 18:59.900
No point in worrying about it.

19:00.810 --> 19:02.820
Lily, are you ready for lunch?

19:03.170 --> 19:04.000
Yeah!

19:04.000 --> 19:05.700
What do you want to eat, Zenos?

19:06.160 --> 19:08.360
I'd be down for a salad!

19:08.360 --> 19:10.250
Lynga wants fish!

19:10.250 --> 19:11.830
Are the two of you insane?

19:11.830 --> 19:14.100
Clearly, we're going to be having meat.

19:15.360 --> 19:17.390
For the record, I wasn't asking you three.

19:17.390 --> 19:19.510
And are you serious about eating here?

19:35.920 --> 19:39.650
Well, I suppose I'll go upstairs and rest.

19:39.920 --> 19:44.160
But keep in mind that you're likely 
the only one in all of the royal capital

19:44.160 --> 19:47.290
capable of getting the slum's leaders in line.

19:47.640 --> 19:50.240
I feel like some kind of 
dangerous animal wrangler.

19:50.240 --> 19:53.330
I really hope we don't end up 
with any more troublesome guests.

19:53.330 --> 19:58.880
"And with those words, Zenos the underground 
healer had sealed his own fate."

19:58.880 --> 20:01.980
Don't just drop ominous lines 
like that before floating off!

20:11.980 --> 20:14.870
Am I really in the slums?

20:16.550 --> 20:18.660
You there. Can I ask you something?

20:18.660 --> 20:20.440
Sure. What's up?

20:20.710 --> 20:24.150
I haven't been in the slums in a while,

20:24.150 --> 20:26.970
and things seem to have changed quite a bit.

20:26.970 --> 20:30.450
You're getting along awfully well 
with the werewolves and orcs.

20:30.450 --> 20:34.290
Well, it turns out they're not 
so bad once you get to know 'em.

20:34.640 --> 20:38.550
But there was so much bad 
blood before. What happened?

20:38.550 --> 20:40.260
Well, y'know...

20:40.530 --> 20:43.320
Look, I don't know who you are,

20:43.320 --> 20:45.300
so I can't really tell you about it.

20:45.300 --> 20:47.760
He's trying to keep a low profile, after all.

20:48.080 --> 20:49.890
A low profile?

20:49.890 --> 20:50.770
See ya.

20:51.520 --> 20:54.640
Hold it. You're going to talk.

20:54.640 --> 20:57.840
And no nonsense. Only answer 
the questions I ask you.

20:57.840 --> 20:59.070
Who's the mediator?

20:59.750 --> 21:01.600
I'm not telling you.

21:01.600 --> 21:04.310
We all owe him a lot.

21:04.310 --> 21:05.560
You can shoot me, but—

21:05.560 --> 21:08.760
This mediator has earned 
quite a bit of loyalty, then.

21:08.760 --> 21:10.330
So, who is he?

21:08.760 --> 21:11.050
Talk about amazing.

21:11.050 --> 21:12.500
Yeah, seriously.

21:11.420 --> 21:12.500
Boss!

21:14.000 --> 21:17.380
<i>Starting trouble in enemy 
territory would be a bad idea.</i>

21:17.680 --> 21:21.090
<i>Their arms should've been injured 
beyond any hope of healing,</i>

21:21.460 --> 21:25.510
<i>but from that glimpse I got, 
they've fully recovered.</i>

21:26.330 --> 21:28.410
<i>How is that possible?</i>

21:29.270 --> 21:32.390
And now, what do I do next?

21:32.390 --> 21:34.620
There are too many things I don't know.

21:35.940 --> 21:37.040
Like where I am.

21:39.810 --> 21:41.980
I'm getting chills for some reason.

21:42.570 --> 21:45.280
Pardon me. I could use some directions.

21:45.880 --> 21:49.780
I was in the slums, but before I knew it, 
I was in an abandoned part of the city.

21:50.140 --> 21:52.800
Yeah? That's rough.

21:52.800 --> 21:56.950
Yes, I'm afraid a bad sense of 
direction is my only real fault.

21:56.950 --> 21:57.790
Is that right?

21:58.080 --> 22:01.220
I noticed someone was in this house, 
so I decided to ask for help.

22:01.220 --> 22:04.010
Can you show me how to get back into town?

22:04.010 --> 22:05.410
Okay, in that case—

22:05.410 --> 22:07.800
Zenos, do we have a patient?

22:07.800 --> 22:09.970
No, just someone who got lost.

22:12.420 --> 22:14.470
It seems I owe you thanks, 
albeit coincidentally.

22:17.560 --> 22:20.230
The tea! Wait, no, Zenos!

22:20.230 --> 22:22.110
Zenos!

23:55.580 --> 24:00.040
A Righteous Hero

23:57.230 --> 23:58.780
"A Righteous Hero."
